## Project Summary

This micro-project demonstrates 1D image blurring using the Heat Equation and Fourier Series. The diffusion of pixel intensity is modeled using a partial differential equation, and Python is used to simulate and visualize the progressive blurring of a sharp edge at different time steps.

The project demonstrates how higher-frequency components decay faster during diffusion, producing a low-pass filtering effect and resulting in image/signal blurring.

